[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity-area station installed for flood warning purposes in 1998. GENERAL: Velocity-area station, about a 4m wide section. Station opened in 1998 as a flood warning level site, one of 3 flow sites on the River Cober. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14). STATION HYDROMETRY: Fairly stable shoal forms a natural bed control at lower flows. Has been subject to change but stable since 2011. The site is not bypassed but is impacted by a public water supply abstraction upstream of the site on the River Cober at Trenear gauging station. Between Trenars gauging station and this site, there is a significant input of about 35% of the catchment flow from the Releath Stream. Rated by gaugings to within 75% of bankfull (1.1m) and extrapolated to bank full. FLOW RECORD: High flow event in 2012 did not change the relationship at high flows. FLOW REGIME: Moderate influence from public water supply abstraction and compensation flows at Trenear gauging station and industrial abstractions. Flows influenced by hstorical mineworkings in the catchment.
CATCHMENT,Igneous catchment, granite with some areas of alluvium. Land use is mostly rural/agricultural/ mining with little urbanisation. No major changes to catchment.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to within 70% of bankfull, extrapolated to bankfull.
Pooling Suitability,Not gauged above bankfull.
[END]
